        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "1e144ddee0fe757996089fd0b0bcfbf81d94510d",
            "parents": [
                "923507c5283ec1325275dac7f2bf0165af40e12f"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/90/88190/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Brad Bishop",
                "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                "username": "bradbishop"
            },
            "createdOn": 1773180114,
            "author": {
                "name": "Brad Bishop",
                "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                "username": "bradbishop"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the cleanup. I think this is a step in the right direction. There\u2019s a delicate balance between offering flexibility and overwhelming users with too many configuration options. It feels like we may have crossed that line long ago, and the current level of configurability is starting to introduce unnecessary complexity and confusion."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "you really wouldn't have to. But thanks for checking."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Since some of these magic numbers were just copied from the meson.options, I'm not sure @bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com how much you can make a better value for them.  It's unfortunate."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> some of these magic numbers\n\nThe intent was to copy -all- the magic numbers from the defaults previously specified in meson.options.  If there is a case where I goofed that up please let me know.\n\nMarking resolved, let me know if there is more I can do here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I can see how the change helps in terms of reducing bloat in the file here, but at the same time these were added as configurable because they really are not fixed. Such options exist elsewhere in openbmc repos as well. Once there is a usecase someone will have to add these back again. Are there other strong reasons/guidelines for removing unused (beyond the default value) configs?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> Such options exist elsewhere in openbmc repos as well\n\nI would open pull requests to remove those as well, but I'm focused on PLDM right now.\n\n> Once there is a usecase someone will have to add these back again.\n\nAssuming it ever happens, which seems unlikely at this point?  And if it did, that wouldn't be terribly difficult would it?\n\nWe don't have dead code without users - are config options really any different?  If anything, the dead config options are worse because they are an interface of sorts.\n\n>  Are there other strong reasons/guidelines for removing unused\n\nYes this is a classic example of overengineering.  There are so many shiny knobs and fancy buttons to push that the whole interface becomes complex and confusing.\n\nI think all of these apply to some level:\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You_aren't_gonna_need_it\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KISS_principle\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worse_is_better\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overengineering"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "\ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/ibm/libpldmresponder/file_io.hpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this number derived from a spec somewhere or anything?  It doesn't seem like a nice power of 2.\n\n```\n8 MiB to byte = 8388608 byte\n```\n\nIs there some way for us to write this as less of a magic number and more of a derivation as to why it was chosen?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/ibm/libpldmresponder/file_io.hpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I will have a look at the git history to see if I can sus out where this came from.  Will tag @manojkiran.eda@gmail.com too to see if he has any idea."
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/ibm/libpldmresponder/file_io.hpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Apparently this is 8MB - 4K.  Last reference I could find was I3118956ac745fdd60499aec18f01e35b7a33c6bd"
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/ibm/libpldmresponder/file_io.hpp",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah , its 8MB-4k. Not sure what that 4k is for \ud83d\ude0a of the top of my head. Will need to check it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a surprising number."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Agreed.  @manojkiran.eda@gmail.com?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/numeric_sensor.cpp",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "999 ms is used as a near 1 second default interval. It behaves like 1 Hz polling. But yeah it could be 1000 too, but i did not press too much as it works and in range."
                }
            ],
